# Earlier evidence-kit versions remain identified by their source commits and
# manifest digests in specs 053, 186, and 188 and the corresponding run reports.
# This version adds the prospectively frozen Term Sheet three-surface
# development kit and makes the existing six-browser grid a standing
# preflight and closeout invariant. It preserves Dinner paper-set attempt 1,
# the fixed element-name assignments, deterministic all-idle completion,
# Dinner judge outputs, and the three-surface Investment Committee design.
# This revision also requires an explicit zero-running-task audit before the
# registered task end and before surveys. Historical runs and their earlier
# manifest digests are not relabeled.
# The prospective Term Sheet revision raises only its hard safety cap from 30
# to 60 minutes and keeps its pre-opened decision alive for two hours. It does
# not change participant guidance, mandates, surfaces, models, extraction,
# blind adjudication, or surveys.
# Spec 191 adds an independently frozen Dinner messages-only sidecar. It does
# not relabel or reopen Dinner's completed three-surface observations.
# The paper-sidecar revision changes no participant guidance. It names watch
# honestly as arrival notification and narrows the mechanical analysis rule so
# assent must concern the primary plan rather than a fallback or side task.
# After the first paper-sidecar judge ignored the transcript-only boundary, the
# judge prompt makes the same boundary explicit as a no-tools/no-repository
# instruction. Its outcome criteria, transcript, and schema are unchanged.
# This revision adds the prospectively frozen Term Sheet messages-only
# development sidecar. It also makes the existing Term Sheet judge and survey
# boundaries explicitly no-tools/no-repository without changing participant
# guidance, outcome criteria, response schemas, or negotiation content.
# This revision adds the prospectively frozen Mafia messages-only development
# sidecar: fixed element-name roles, three no-decision rooms, a task-required
# neutral moderator, and frozen extraction, judgment, survey, and rubric files.
# This revision adds Mafia's prospective three-GRP-surface development kit:
# decisions-disabled chat, natural GRP, and one pre-opened Day 1 plurality
# decision. Its completed messages-only history remains separate and unchanged.
# The structured-Mafia setup correction keeps participant guidance unchanged,
# makes Mica an observer in the private role rooms, and requires named day seats
# to join before the exact Day 1 electorate is opened.
# This revision adds the independently runnable Investment Committee
# messages-only surface and aligns the paper sequence with the principal's
# decision to run the committee before deciding on a full Publishing House
# comparison. No committee task fact, mandate, GRP-room setting, option,
# extractor, judge, survey, model, effort, cap, or completion rule changes.
# This revision adds the prospectively frozen Publishing House four-observation
# paper kit. Prior canonical and Stage A/B runs remain development history; the
# principal waived a duplicate rehearsal block. The four fresh arms share one
# neutral company seed, fixed six element-name roles, three-room topology,
# 75-minute safety cap, extraction, judge, survey, and rubric.
